---
/* oberrieden.pub/follow -> a choice of Instagram or Facebook.

   The target of the "Follow us" code on the printed banner. The banner once
   pointed at /instagram alone; the pub has had a Facebook page on the site
   since, and a guest should get to pick. /instagram still redirects straight
   through, so anything already printed with it keeps working.

   One page for both languages, because both strips of the banner carry the
   same code. Kept short for the same reason as /review: a short URL makes a
   less dense QR code that scans from further away. If either link changes,
   pub.ts changes and nothing has to be reprinted.

   Deliberately not built on Base.astro: someone arriving from a QR code wants
   two buttons, not the menu, hours and photos. It borrows the site's colours,
   two of its fonts and the same brand marks.

   The landlord at the taps heads the page, in a column with the links below
   him, not behind them. As a background his face ended up under the buttons
   and the photo lost its character. The bottom of the photo fades into the
   maroon so the heading can sit on the fade. At phone width the whole page,
   face included, fits on one screen without scrolling.

   The photo is a cleaned-up version of the original (lens flare off the tap
   badges), 929 px wide: enough for the 480 px column at twice the density.
   His consent covers it; nobody else is in the frame. */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import { pub } from "../../data/pub";
import landlord from "../../assets/photos/landlord-taps.jpg";
---

<html lang="de-CH">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Big Ben Pub · Folgen Sie uns / Follow us</title>
    <style>
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Bitter";
        src: url("/fonts/bitter-700-latin.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 700;
        font-display: swap;
      }
      @font-face {
        font-family: "Cabin";
        src: url("/fonts/cabin-600-latin.woff2") format("woff2");
        font-weight: 600;
        font-display: swap;
      }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: center;
        background: #531c23;
        color: #f0e8dc;
        font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, Arial, sans-serif;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .page { width: 100%; max-width: 480px }
      /* Where the column is the full width of the screen, the photo starts
         at the top edge. Centred, it left a band of maroon above it. */
      @media (max-width: 480px) {
        body { align-items: flex-start }
      }
      /* The photo fades to the page's maroon over its lower part, so the
         heading below can overlap it without a hard edge. */
      .photo { position: relative; margin: 0 }
      .photo :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto }
      .photo::after {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        background: linear-gradient(rgba(83,28,35,0) 52%, rgba(83,28,35,.75) 78%, #531c23 100%);
      }
      main {
        position: relative;
        margin: -76px auto 0;
        padding: 0 16px 24px;
        max-width: 360px;
      }
      .pub {
        margin: 0 0 6px;
        font: 600 13px/1.4 Cabin, system-ui, sans-serif;
        letter-spacing: .18em;
        color: #ddba7a;
      }
      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 22px;
        font: 700 28px/1.25 Bitter, Georgia, serif;
        text-shadow: 0 1px 6px rgba(30,22,17,.6);
      }
      h1 span { display: block; font-size: 20px; color: #ddba7a }
      ul { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 14px }
      a.choice {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 14px;
        padding: 14px 18px;
        border-radius: 12px;
        background: #fbf7f0;
        color: #531c23;
        text-decoration: none;
        font: 600 18px/1.3 Cabin, system-ui, sans-serif;
        text-align: left;
      }
      a.choice:hover, a.choice:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #ddba7a; outline-offset: 2px }
      a.choice small { display: block; font: 400 14px/1.3 system-ui, sans-serif; color: #8a6239 }
      /* The same coloured marks as the site's hero and footer: Instagram's
         gradient tile with the camera in white, Facebook's blue disc with a
         white spot behind the f. */
      a.choice :global(.icon) { flex: none; width: 40px; height: 40px }
      a[href*="instagram.com"] :global(.icon) {
        box-sizing: border-box; padding: 6px; border-radius: 12px; color: #fff;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 107%,#fdf497 0%,#fdf497 5%,#fd5949 45%,#d6249f 60%,#285aeb 90%);
      }
      a[href*="facebook.com"] :global(.icon) {
        color: #1877f2; background: radial-gradient(circle,#fff 0 55%,transparent 56%);
      }
      .site { margin: 22px 0 0; font-size: 15px }
      .site a { color: #ddba7a }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="page">
      <figure class="photo">
        <Image
          src={landlord}
          alt="Der Wirt zapft ein Bier im Big Ben Pub."
          widths={[480, 929]}
          sizes="(max-width: 480px) 100vw, 480px"
          format="avif"
          quality={72}
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>
      <main>
        <p class="pub">BIG BEN PUB · OBERRIEDEN</p>
        <h1>Folgen Sie uns <span lang="en">Follow us</span></h1>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a class="choice" href={pub.instagram}>
              <Icon name="instagram" />
              <span>Instagram<small>{pub.instagramHandle}</small></span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="choice" href={pub.facebook}>
              <Icon name="facebook" />
              <span>Facebook<small>Big Ben Pub Oberrieden</small></span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="site"><a href="/">oberrieden.pub</a></p>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
